ionAxis%22%3A%222%22%7D%2C%7B%22dimensionId%22%3A%22Series%22%2C%22dimensionAxis%22%3A%220%22%7D%2C%7B%22dimensionId%22%3A%22Time%22%2C%22dimensionAxis%22%3A%222%22%7D%5D%2C%22NoOfRowsPerPage%22%3A%22250%22%2C%22ShowNotes%22%3Atrue%2C%22EmptyFormat%22%3A%22..%22%2C%22ReportLevelScale%22%3Atrue%2C%22Scale%22%3A%221%22%2C%22Precision%22%3A%220.000%22%2C%22ThousandSeparator%22%3Atrue%2C%22ReportHeader%22%3A%22*The%20figures%20in%20this%20table%20have%20been%20rounded%20for%20presentation%20purposes.%20Data%20with%20greater%20precision%20can%20be%20obtained%20from%20the%20World%20Bank%5Cu0027s%20DataBank%20-%20ICP%202021%20database%20by%20clicking%20on%20the%20following%20link%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fdatabank.worldbank.org%2Fsource%2Ficp-2021%2F.%22%2C%22ReportFooter%22%3A%22%22%2C%22AdvancedOptions%22%3A%7B%22Hierarchy%22%3A%22NONE%22%2C%22RolloverDirection%22%3A%22none%22%2C%22RolloverInterval%22%3Anull%2C%22HideEmptyRow%22%3Afalse%2C%22HideEmptyColumn%22%3Afalse%7D%2C%22ReportNotes%22%3A%22Results%20from%20the%20International%20Comparison%20Program%20(Benchmark)%202021%20cycle%20include%20data%20for%20the%20new%20reference%20year%202021%2C%20revised%20data%20for%20the%20previous%20reference%20year%202017%2C%20and%20purchasing%20power%20parities%20(PPPs)%20time%20series%20for%202018%20to%202020.%202021%20results%20are%20available%20for%20176%20participating%20economies%20and%20their%20aggregate%20regions.%20They%20cover%2045%20expenditure%20headings%20and%20provide%20several%20indicators%20for%20each%20heading%2C%20including%20PPPs%2C%20national%20accounts%20expenditures%20in%20PPP%20and%20nominal%20terms%2C%20and%20price%20level%20indices.%20Imputed%20results%20are%20available%20for%20an%20additional%2019%20economies%20that%20did%20not%20participate%20in%20the%20ICP%202021%20cycle.%20Revised%202017%20results%20are%20available%20for%20178%20participating%20economies%20and%20cover%2044%20expenditure%20headings%20and%20several%20indicators%2C%20including%20PPPs%2C%20national%20accounts%20expenditures%20in%20PPP%20and%20nominal%20terms%2C%20and%20price%20level%20indices.%20Additionally%2C%20imputed%20results%20are%20available%20for%2017%20economies%20that%20did%20not%20participate%20in%20the%20ICP%202017%20cycle.%20Annual%20PPPs%20are%20available%20for%202017%20to%202021%20and%20cover%206%20major%20expenditure%20headings.%202022-2023%20GDP%20PPP%20series%20are%20also%20provided%20beyond%20the%20most%20recent%20ICP%20benchmark%20based%20on%20the%20standard%20extrapolation%20approach.%20PPPs%20are%20statistical%20estimates%20and%20should%20be%20treated%20as%20approximations%20of%20true%20values%2C%20subject%20to%20sampling%2C%20measurement%2C%20and%20classification%20errors.%20They%20should%20not%20be%20used%20as%20indicators%20of%20currency%20under-%20or%20overvaluation.%20ICP%20Results%20are%20based%20on%20data%20supplied%20by%20participating%20economies%20to%20the%20global%20and%20regional%20implementing%20agencies%2C%20and%20produced%20in%20accordance%20with%20ICP%20methodology.%20Results%20are%20not%20deemed%20to%20be%20national%20official%20statistics.%20The%20standard%20ICP%20methodology%20between%20the%20two%20most%20recent%202017%20and%202021%20ICP%20cycles%20has%20been%20maintained.%20However%2C%20in%20ICP%202021%2C%20the%20Commonwealth%20of%20Independent%20States%20(CIS)%20region%20was%20linked%20through%20the%20standard%20global%20core%20list%20approach%2C%20unlike%20in%20ICP%202017%2C%20when%20the%20CIS%20region%20was%20linked%20through%20the%20Russian%20Federation%2C%20which%20participated%20in%20both%20the%20OECD%20and%20CIS%20comparisons.%20For%20ICP%202017%2C%20the%20Russian%20Federation%20results%20are%20based%20on%20the%20OECD%20comparison%2C%20and%20for%20ICP%202021%2C%20they%20are%20based%20on%20the%20CIS%20comparison.%20Furthermore%2C%20the%20Asia%20and%20Pacific%20region%20moved%20to%20the%20standard%20ICP%20approach%20for%20estimating%20housing%20PPPs%20based%20on%20rental%20and%20volume%20data%20during%20the%20ICP%202021%20cycle.%20The%20standard%20approach%20was%20utilized%20for%20the%20revised%20ICP%202017%20results%20and%20ICP%202021%20results%2C%20both%20at%20the%20regional%20and%20global%20levels%2C%20instead%20of%20the%20previously%20utilized%20reference%20volume%20approach.%201%2F%20PPPs%20are%20statistical%20estimates%20and%20should%20be%20treated%20as%20approximations%20of%20true%20values%2C%20subject%20to%20sampling%2C%20measurement%2C%20and%20classification%20errors.%20They%20should%20not%20be%20used%20as%20indicators%20of%20currency%20under-%20or%20overvaluation.%20ICP%20Results%20are%20based%20on%20data%20supplied%20by%20participating%20economies%20to%20the%20global%20and%20regional%20implementing%20agencies%2C%20and%20produced%20in%20accordance%20with%20ICP%20methodology.%20Results%20are%20not%20deemed%20to%20be%20national%20official%20statistics.%202%2F%20The%20standard%20ICP%20methodology%20between%20the%20two%20most%20recent%202017%20and%202021%20ICP%20cycles%20has%20been%20maintained.%20However%2C%20in%20ICP%202021%2C%20the%20Commonwealth%20of%20Independent%20States%20(CIS)%20region%20was%20linked%20through%20the%20standard%20global%20core%20list%20approach%2C%20unlike%20in%20ICP%202017%2C%20when%20the%20CIS%20region%20was%20linked%20through%20the%20Russian%20Federation%2C%20which%20participated%20in%20both%20the%20OECD%20and%20CIS%20comparisons.%20For%20ICP%202017%2C%20the%20Russian%20Federation%20results%20are%20based%20on%20the%20OECD%20comparison%2C%20and%20for%20ICP%202021%2C%20they%20are%20based%20on%20the%20CIS%20comparison.%20Furthermore%2C%20the%20Asia%20and%20Pacific%20region%20moved%20to%20the%20standard%20ICP%20approach%20for%20estimating%20housing%20PPPs%20based%20on%20rental%20and%20volume%20data%20during%20the%20ICP%202021%20cycle.%20The%20standard%20approach%20was%20utilized%20for%20the%20revised%20ICP%202017%20results%20and%20ICP%202021%20results%2C%20both%20at%20the%20regional%20and%20global%20levels%2C%20instead%20of%20the%20previously%20utilized%20reference%20volume%20approach.%20For%20the%20time%20series%20estimates%20for%202018-2020%2C%20data%20were%20complemented%20with%20internal%20estimates%20by%20ICP%20Global%20Office%20where%20participating%20economies%20could%20not%20provide%20any%20of%20input%20data%20required%20for%20PPPs%20time%20series%20estimates.%22%7D&hdnSelectVars=%5B%7B%22controlid%22%3A%22DBList%22%2C%22memberdetails%22%3A%5B%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%223869%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22ICP%202021%22%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%5D%2C%22aggregationruleall%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22controlid%22%3A%22Country%22%2C%22memberdetails%22%3A%5B%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BEAB%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22East%20Asia%20%26%20Pacific%20(Benchmark)%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BAUS%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22Australia%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BBRN%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22Brunei%20Darussalam%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BKHM%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22Cambodia%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BCHN%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22China%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BFJI%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22Fiji%22%2C%22iscustom%22%3Afalse%2C%22customdefinition%22%3Anull%2C%22AggregationRule%22%3Anull%7D%2C%7B%22uniquename%22%3A%22%5BCountry%5D.%5BList%5D.%26%5BHKG%5D%22%2C%22displayname%22%3A%22Hong%20Kong%20SAR%2C%20China%22%2C%22is